    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auspĭcālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to divination</i>, <i>suitable for auguries</i>, <i>auspicial</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pisciculus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 1, 1, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mamert. Pan. Maxim. 6</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auspĭ-cālĭter</span></b>  =
			auspicato, <i>with the appropriate taking of
			auguries</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ponere gromam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Limit. Constit. p. 153</span></i>
			 Goes.</div>
